Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection();
conn.setAutoCommit(false); // disable auto-commit for batch efficiency

String sql = "INSERT INTO products (name, price) VALUES (?, ?)";
try (PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql)) {

    for (Product p : products) {
        ps.setString(1, p.getName());
        ps.setDouble(2, p.getPrice());
        ps.addBatch(); // queue this row

        // flush every 500 rows to avoid memory buildup
        if (counter % 500 == 0) {
            ps.executeBatch();
            ps.clearBatch();
        }
    }

    ps.executeBatch(); // execute remaining
    conn.commit();

} catch (SQLException e) {
    conn.rollback();
    throw e;
} finally {
    conn.setAutoCommit(true);
    conn.close();
}
```

**Why batch is faster:**
- Single network round trip instead of N round trips
- Database processes INSERT statements more efficiently in bulk
- Transaction spans all inserts: all succeed or all roll back

